      "content": "The grief you feel is valid and real, stemming from the loss of the confident version of yourself, but don't confuse this profound loss of function with the loss of your soul; your inner self remains intact even when the physical expression fractures. Healing often requires redefining your identity beyond those specific abilities, finding new ways to inhabit this body that haven't been blocked by your old limitations. Please consider speaking with a therapist who can help you navigate this disassociation without feeling like a ghost in your own skin.",
